// REJECTS: Field 'mappings' should be specified only once
//
// `mappings:` may appear at most once on a Runtime. The grammar says `(mappings |
// connections | connectionStoresList)*` -- a star, so any number of each -- and the
// singularity is enforced afterwards by the walker.
//
// Repetition is a plausible thing to write, because the field's value is already a LIST:
// two mappings blocks reads as an obvious shorthand for one longer list, and a rewrite that
// accumulates as it loops implements exactly that without deciding to. It then silently
// keeps the first, or the last, or both -- three engines, three answers.
###Runtime
Runtime fixture::neg::TwoMappings
{
   mappings:
   [
      fixture::neg::PersonMapping
   ];
   mappings:
   [
      fixture::neg::FirmMapping
   ];
}
